  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What are the four processes of coastal erosion?', 'Hydraulic action, abrasion, attrition and solution.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is hydraulic action?', 'Waves force air into cracks in the cliff, which breaks the rock apart.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is abrasion?', 'Rocks carried by waves are thrown against the cliff, wearing it away.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is attrition?', 'Rocks carried by waves knock against each other, becoming smaller and rounder.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is solution?', 'Seawater dissolves soluble rocks such as chalk and limestone.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is longshore drift?', 'The movement of sediment along the coast by waves approaching at an angle.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is the swash?', 'The movement of water up the beach after a wave breaks.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is the backwash?', 'The movement of water back down the beach under gravity.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a constructive wave?', 'A low, gentle wave with a strong swash and weak backwash, which builds up beaches.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a destructive wave?', 'A tall, steep wave with a weak swash and strong backwash, which erodes beaches.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is fetch?', 'The distance over which the wind blows across open water, affecting wave size.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'How is a headland formed?', 'Resistant rock erodes more slowly than softer rock, leaving land sticking out into the sea.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'How is a bay formed?', 'Softer rock is eroded more quickly, forming a curved inlet between headlands.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'How is a stack formed?', 'Waves erode a crack into a cave, then an arch; the arch roof collapses, leaving a stack.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a stump?', 'The remains of a stack after it has been eroded further.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a wave-cut platform?', 'A flat area of rock at the base of a cliff, left as the cliff retreats through erosion.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'How is a spit formed?', 'Longshore drift carries sediment past a bend in the coastline, where it is deposited in the sea.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a bar?', 'A spit that grows across a bay, joining two headlands and sometimes trapping a lagoon.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a beach?', 'A deposit of sand and shingle along the coast, formed by constructive waves.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a sand dune?', 'A hill of sand formed when wind blows sand inland, trapped by vegetation such as marram grass.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is hard engineering?', 'Building artificial structures to control the sea, e.g. sea walls, groynes and rock armour.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is soft engineering?', 'Working with natural processes to manage the coast, e.g. beach nourishment and dune regeneration.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a sea wall?', 'A concrete wall that reflects waves back out to sea; effective but expensive.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is a groyne?', 'A wooden or rock barrier built out to sea to trap sediment moved by longshore drift.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is rock armour?', 'Large boulders placed at the foot of a cliff to absorb wave energy.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is beach nourishment?', 'Adding sand or shingle to a beach to make it wider, absorbing wave energy.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is managed retreat?', 'Allowing the coast to erode or flood naturally in low-value areas.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Eduqas', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Coasts and Coastal Management', 'What is sea-level rise''s effect on coasts?', 'It increases flooding and erosion, threatening homes, farmland and habitats.', 28),
