  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Global Circulation and Climate Change', 'What is sea-level rise caused by?', 'Melting ice sheets and glaciers, and thermal expansion of water.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Global Circulation and Climate Change', 'What is thermal expansion?', 'Water expanding as it warms, raising sea levels.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Global Circulation and Climate Change', 'What is the Quaternary period?', 'The last 2.6 million years, with glacial and interglacial periods.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.1', 'Global Circulation and Climate Change', 'What is an interglacial period?', 'A warmer period between glacial periods.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What scale measures tropical cyclone strength?', 'The Saffir–Simpson scale, from category 1 to 5.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What wind speed is a category 5 cyclone?', '252 km/h or more.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Name five physical hazards of tropical cyclones.', 'High winds, intense rainfall, storm surges, coastal flooding and landslides.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Which cyclone hazard usually kills the most people?', 'The storm surge.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'When did Hurricane Katrina hit New Orleans?', '29 August 2005.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Why was New Orleans so vulnerable?', 'Much of the city is below sea level between Lake Pontchartrain and the Mississippi.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What happened to New Orleans'' levees in Katrina?', 'They failed in over 50 places, flooding about 80% of the city.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How many people died in Hurricane Katrina?', 'About 1,800; over 1 million were displaced.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How much damage did Katrina cause?', 'About $125 billion.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Why was the Katrina response criticised?', 'The federal (FEMA) response was slow and poorer residents without cars were left behind.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How has New Orleans been protected since Katrina?', 'About $14.5 billion on stronger levees, a surge barrier and huge pumping stations.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Compare deaths in Katrina and Haiyan.', 'About 1,800 in Katrina (USA) vs over 6,300 in Haiyan (Philippines).', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Why are economic losses higher in developed countries?', 'Buildings, infrastructure and property are worth more.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Give two factors that make a country vulnerable to cyclones.', 'Low-lying coasts or deltas, and poverty (weak housing, few shelters).', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What sea temperature do tropical storms need?', 'At least 26–27°C.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Why don''t tropical storms form at the Equator?', 'The Coriolis effect is too weak to make the air spin.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What powers a tropical storm?', 'Latent heat released as water vapour condenses in rising air.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What is the eye of a tropical storm?', 'The calm, clear centre with sinking air and the lowest pressure.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What is the eye wall?', 'The ring of tall cloud around the eye, with the strongest winds and heaviest rain.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Why do tropical storms weaken over land?', 'They lose their supply of warm, moist air and are slowed by friction.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What is a storm surge?', 'A rise in sea level caused by strong winds and low pressure pushing water onshore.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How might climate change affect tropical storm intensity?', 'More storms are likely to reach the highest categories, with heavier rain.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How might climate change affect tropical storm distribution?', 'Storms may form further from the tropics as more ocean reaches 26–27°C.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'When and where did Typhoon Haiyan strike?', 'November 2013, the Philippines — especially Tacloban on Leyte.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How many people died in Typhoon Haiyan?', 'Over 6,300, with around 1,000 more missing.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'How high was Haiyan''s storm surge?', 'Up to 5–6 metres in Tacloban.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Give a secondary effect of Typhoon Haiyan.', 'Food and water shortages led to disease and looting; 6 million people lost their income.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Give a long-term response to Typhoon Haiyan.', 'Build Back Better reconstruction, cash-for-work, new cyclone shelters and mangrove replanting.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'What are the four ways of reducing tropical storm effects?', 'Monitoring, prediction, protection and planning.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.2', 'Tropical Cyclones', 'Give an example of protection against tropical storms.', 'Raised cyclone shelters in Bangladesh, storm-surge barriers or buildings on stilts.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the structure of the Earth?', 'Crust, mantle, outer core and inner core.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a tectonic plate?', 'A large section of the Earth''s crust that moves slowly on the mantle.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What causes plates to move?', 'Convection currents in the mantle, and slab pull.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a destructive plate margin?', 'Where an oceanic plate is forced under a continental plate, causing earthquakes and violent volcanoes.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a constructive plate margin?', 'Where plates move apart and magma rises to form new crust, causing gentle volcanoes.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a conservative plate margin?', 'Where plates slide past each other, causing earthquakes but no volcanoes.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a collision margin?', 'Where two continental plates collide, forming fold mountains.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the focus of an earthquake?', 'The point underground where the earthquake starts.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the epicentre?', 'The point on the surface directly above the focus.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How are earthquakes measured?', 'Using the moment magnitude scale (or Richter scale) and a seismometer.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a composite volcano?', 'A steep-sided volcano made of layers of ash and lava, with explosive eruptions.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a shield volcano?', 'A wide, gently sloping volcano made of runny lava, with gentle eruptions.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a hotspot?', 'An area of volcanic activity away from plate margins, e.g. Hawaii.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the primary effects of earthquakes?', 'Buildings collapse, roads and bridges are damaged, and people are killed or injured.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the secondary effects of earthquakes?', 'Fires, tsunamis, landslides, disease, and homelessness.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a tsunami?', 'A large sea wave caused by an earthquake under the ocean.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the primary effects of volcanoes?', 'Lava flows, pyroclastic flows, ash falls and gas emissions.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What are the secondary effects of volcanoes?', 'Lahars (mudflows), flooding, loss of tourism, and fertile soils in the long term.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Why do people live near volcanoes?', 'Fertile soils, tourism, geothermal energy and minerals.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How can the effects of earthquakes be reduced?', 'Earthquake-proof buildings, education, emergency plans, and early warning systems.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is an earthquake-proof building?', 'A building designed to withstand shaking, e.g. with deep foundations, cross-bracing and shock absorbers.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'How can volcanic eruptions be predicted?', 'Monitoring ground swelling, gas emissions and small earthquakes.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Why do earthquakes have more impact in poorer countries?', 'Poor-quality buildings, fewer emergency services, and less preparation.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Give an example of an earthquake in a richer country.', 'Japan (Tōhoku 2011) or Christchurch, New Zealand (2011).', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'Give an example of an earthquake in a poorer country.', 'Nepal (2015) or Haiti (2010).', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the Pacific Ring of Fire?', 'A zone around the Pacific Ocean with many volcanoes and earthquakes.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a pyroclastic flow?', 'A fast-moving cloud of hot gas, ash and rock.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is a lahar?', 'A mudflow of volcanic material mixed with water.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is hazard mapping?', 'Mapping areas at risk from hazards to plan land use and evacuation.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Tectonic Hazards', 'What is the magnitude of an earthquake?', 'A measure of the energy released by an earthquake.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What does Rostow''s model show?', 'Five stages of economic growth: traditional society to high mass consumption.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'Name Rostow''s five stages.', 'Traditional society, pre-conditions for take-off, take-off, drive to maturity, high mass consumption.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'Give a criticism of Rostow''s model.', 'It is based on Western countries and ignores colonialism and unequal trade.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is Frank''s dependency theory?', 'A rich core keeps the poor periphery underdeveloped through unequal trade, debt and aid.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What does the Gini coefficient measure?', 'Income inequality within a country, from 0 (equal) to 1 (unequal).', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'When did India open its economy?', '1991 economic reforms.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'Why do TNCs invest in India?', 'A large, young, English-speaking workforce, lower costs and a huge market.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is top-down vs bottom-up development?', 'Top-down: large government-led projects; bottom-up: small community-led projects.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is development?', 'The process of improving people''s standard of living and quality of life.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is GNI per capita?', 'Gross national income divided by the population, a measure of average wealth.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is the Human Development Index?', 'A measure of development combining life expectancy, education and income.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is life expectancy?', 'The average number of years a person is expected to live.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is literacy rate?', 'The percentage of adults who can read and write.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is infant mortality rate?', 'The number of babies who die before their first birthday per 1000 live births.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is a low-income country (developing country)?', 'A poorer country with lower development, e.g. Malawi.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is a newly emerging economy (emerging country)?', 'A country experiencing rapid economic growth, e.g. India or Brazil.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is the development gap?', 'The difference in wealth and quality of life between richer and poorer countries.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What are the causes of uneven development?', 'Physical factors (climate, disasters), economic factors (trade, debt) and historical factors (colonialism).', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'How does trade affect development?', 'Countries exporting low-value primary products earn less than those exporting manufactured goods.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is aid?', 'Help given by one country or organisation to another, e.g. money, food or expertise.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is short-term aid?', 'Emergency help after a disaster, e.g. food, shelter and medicine.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is long-term aid?', 'Help to improve development over time, e.g. building schools and wells.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is fair trade?', 'A system ensuring producers in poorer countries receive a fair price and good working conditions.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is debt relief?', 'Cancelling some of a country''s debt so it can spend more on development.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is microfinance?', 'Small loans to people in poorer countries to start businesses.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is intermediate technology?', 'Simple, affordable technology suited to local needs, e.g. water pumps.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is a multinational company?', 'A company that operates in more than one country.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What are the advantages of TNCs to poorer countries?', 'Jobs, investment, skills and infrastructure.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What are the disadvantages of TNCs to poorer countries?', 'Low wages, poor conditions, profits going abroad, and environmental damage.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Development Dynamics', 'What is the Demographic Transition Model?', 'A model showing how birth and death rates change as a country develops.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a world city?', 'A city with global influence in finance, trade, culture and politics, e.g. London or Tokyo.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'How many megacities were there in 1950?', 'Two — New York and Tokyo.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is re-urbanisation?', 'People moving back into regenerated city centres.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'Give a top-down strategy in Mumbai.', 'The Dharavi Redevelopment Project (Adani Group) or new metro lines and the Coastal Road.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'Give a bottom-up strategy in Mumbai.', 'SPARC and Mahila Milan women''s savings groups building community toilets.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'Why do some Dharavi residents oppose redevelopment?', 'They fear losing homes, workshops and community, or being excluded.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is urbanisation?', 'The increase in the proportion of people living in towns and cities.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a megacity?', 'A city with a population of more than 10 million.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What causes urbanisation?', 'Rural–urban migration and natural increase.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What are push factors?', 'Reasons that make people leave rural areas, e.g. lack of jobs, poor services and natural disasters.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What are pull factors?', 'Reasons that attract people to cities, e.g. jobs, better healthcare and education.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is natural increase?', 'When the birth rate is higher than the death rate.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'Where is urbanisation happening fastest?', 'In lower-income and newly emerging countries in Africa and Asia.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a squatter settlement?', 'An area of poor-quality housing built illegally on land the residents don''t own.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What are the problems of squatter settlements?', 'Poor sanitation, lack of clean water, disease, crime, and flood or fire risk.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is the informal economy?', 'Jobs that aren''t officially recorded or taxed, e.g. street selling.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a site-and-service scheme?', 'Authorities provide land with basic services, and residents build their own homes.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is self-help housing?', 'Residents are given materials and support to improve their own homes.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is suburbanisation?', 'The movement of people from the inner city to the suburbs.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is counter-urbanisation?', 'The movement of people from cities to rural areas.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a global city?', 'A city with major international influence in finance, culture and politics, e.g. London or New York.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What are the challenges of rapid urbanisation?', 'Housing shortages, traffic, pollution, unemployment and pressure on services.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is urban sprawl?', 'The spread of cities into the surrounding countryside.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a brownfield site?', 'Previously developed land that can be reused.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a greenfield site?', 'Land that hasn''t been built on before.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is a sustainable city?', 'A city that meets people''s needs without damaging the environment for future generations.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'Give an example of a sustainable urban feature.', 'Public transport, green spaces, recycling schemes and energy-efficient buildings.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is the CBD?', 'The central business district, the commercial centre of a city.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is the inner city?', 'The area around the CBD, often with older housing and industry.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Challenges of an Urbanising World', 'What is the rural–urban fringe?', 'The area where the city meets the countryside.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How does igneous rock form?', 'From cooled magma or lava — hard rocks such as granite and basalt.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How does sedimentary rock form?', 'From layers of sediment compressed over time, e.g. chalk, clay and limestone.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How does metamorphic rock form?', 'Existing rock changed by heat and pressure, e.g. slate and schist.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a Shoreline Management Plan?', 'A plan dividing the coast into sections, each given an option such as hold the line or managed realignment.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'Name the four SMP options.', 'Hold the line, advance the line, managed realignment and no active intervention.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'Why can coastal defences cause conflict?', 'They can starve beaches downdrift of sediment, increasing erosion elsewhere.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What are the four processes of coastal erosion?', 'Hydraulic action, abrasion, attrition and solution.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is hydraulic action?', 'Waves force air into cracks in the cliff, which breaks the rock apart.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is abrasion?', 'Rocks carried by waves are thrown against the cliff, wearing it away.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is attrition?', 'Rocks carried by waves knock against each other, becoming smaller and rounder.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is solution?', 'Seawater dissolves soluble rocks such as chalk and limestone.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is longshore drift?', 'The movement of sediment along the coast by waves approaching at an angle.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is the swash?', 'The movement of water up the beach after a wave breaks.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is the backwash?', 'The movement of water back down the beach under gravity.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a constructive wave?', 'A low, gentle wave with a strong swash and weak backwash, which builds up beaches.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a destructive wave?', 'A tall, steep wave with a weak swash and strong backwash, which erodes beaches.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is fetch?', 'The distance over which the wind blows across open water, affecting wave size.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How is a headland formed?', 'Resistant rock erodes more slowly than softer rock, leaving land sticking out into the sea.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How is a bay formed?', 'Softer rock is eroded more quickly, forming a curved inlet between headlands.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How is a stack formed?', 'Waves erode a crack into a cave, then an arch; the arch roof collapses, leaving a stack.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a stump?', 'The remains of a stack after it has been eroded further.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a wave-cut platform?', 'A flat area of rock at the base of a cliff, left as the cliff retreats through erosion.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'How is a spit formed?', 'Longshore drift carries sediment past a bend in the coastline, where it is deposited in the sea.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a bar?', 'A spit that grows across a bay, joining two headlands and sometimes trapping a lagoon.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a beach?', 'A deposit of sand and shingle along the coast, formed by constructive waves.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a sand dune?', 'A hill of sand formed when wind blows sand inland, trapped by vegetation such as marram grass.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is hard engineering?', 'Building artificial structures to control the sea, e.g. sea walls, groynes and rock armour.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is soft engineering?', 'Working with natural processes to manage the coast, e.g. beach nourishment and dune regeneration.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a sea wall?', 'A concrete wall that reflects waves back out to sea; effective but expensive.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.1', 'UK Physical Landscapes and Coastal Change', 'What is a groyne?', 'A wooden or rock barrier built out to sea to trap sediment moved by longshore drift.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is the source of a river?', 'Where the river begins, often in upland areas.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is the mouth of a river?', 'Where the river meets the sea or a lake.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a tributary?', 'A smaller river that joins a larger one.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a confluence?', 'The point where two rivers meet.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a drainage basin?', 'The area of land drained by a river and its tributaries.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a watershed?', 'The boundary of a drainage basin, usually high ground.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'How does a river change from source to mouth?', 'It becomes wider and deeper, with a greater discharge and gentler gradient.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is vertical erosion?', 'Erosion that deepens the river channel, common in the upper course.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is lateral erosion?', 'Erosion that widens the river channel, common in the middle and lower course.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What are the four types of river transportation?', 'Traction, saltation, suspension and solution.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is traction?', 'Large boulders are rolled along the river bed.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is saltation?', 'Small pebbles bounce along the river bed.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is suspension?', 'Fine particles are carried in the water.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'When does a river deposit sediment?', 'When it loses energy, e.g. when it slows down on the inside of a bend or enters the sea.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'How is a waterfall formed?', 'Soft rock beneath hard rock is eroded, creating an overhang that collapses; the waterfall retreats, leaving a gorge.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a gorge?', 'A steep-sided valley formed as a waterfall retreats upstream.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a V-shaped valley?', 'A steep valley in the upper course, formed by vertical erosion and weathering.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is interlocking spurs?', 'Hills that stick out alternately on either side of a river in the upper course.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'How is a meander formed?', 'Erosion on the outside of a bend (fast flow) and deposition on the inside (slow flow).', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'How is an oxbow lake formed?', 'Erosion narrows the neck of a meander until the river cuts through it during a flood; deposition seals off the old loop.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a floodplain?', 'Flat land either side of a river in the lower course, covered with deposits during floods.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a levée?', 'A raised bank along a river, formed by deposition of sediment during floods.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a hydrograph?', 'A graph showing river discharge over time, often in relation to rainfall.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is lag time?', 'The time between peak rainfall and peak discharge.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What factors increase flood risk?', 'Heavy rainfall, impermeable rock, steep slopes, urbanisation and deforestation.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'How does urbanisation increase flood risk?', 'Impermeable surfaces increase surface runoff, and drains carry water quickly to rivers.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a flood defence?', 'A structure or strategy to reduce flooding, e.g. dams, embankments, flood relief channels.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is a flood relief channel?', 'An artificial channel that diverts water away from a town when river levels are high.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is river restoration?', 'Returning a river to a more natural state to reduce flood risk and improve habitats.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.2', 'River Processes and Pressures', 'What is flood zoning?', 'Restricting building on floodplains in areas at high risk of flooding.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a core region?', 'An area with high population, jobs and income, e.g. London and the South East.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a peripheral region?', 'A remote area with low population, fewer jobs and ageing population, e.g. the Scottish Highlands.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What share of UK jobs are in services?', 'Over 80%.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'How has migration affected UK population?', 'It is a major part of population growth and brings a younger workforce.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'How has online shopping affected high streets?', 'Fewer shoppers and many shop closures.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'Give an example of an urban–rural link.', 'Commuting from villages into cities, or cities using rural reservoirs and recreation.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is the UK''s population distribution?', 'Most people live in cities and the south-east of England, with lower densities in upland areas.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is deindustrialisation?', 'The decline of manufacturing industry.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What caused deindustrialisation in UK cities?', 'Competition from cheaper overseas producers, automation, and the decline of coal and steel.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is the post-industrial economy?', 'An economy based on services, finance, research and IT rather than manufacturing.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a science park?', 'A group of high-tech businesses located near a university.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is urban deprivation?', 'A lack of access to jobs, services and good housing in parts of a city.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is the Index of Multiple Deprivation?', 'A measure of deprivation using income, employment, health, education, crime, housing and environment.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is urban regeneration?', 'Improving run-down urban areas to attract people and businesses.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'Give an example of a UK regeneration project.', 'London Docklands, Cardiff Bay, or Manchester''s Salford Quays.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is Cardiff Bay regeneration?', 'Redevelopment of the old docks into a waterfront area with offices, housing, the Senedd and leisure facilities.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What are the benefits of regeneration?', 'New jobs, improved environment, better housing and increased investment.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What are the problems of regeneration?', 'Rising house prices may push out original residents, and not all benefit.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a retail park?', 'A group of large stores on the edge of a town, with free parking.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'Why have high streets declined?', 'Online shopping, out-of-town retail parks and high rents.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a commuter?', 'Someone who travels from where they live to work in another place.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a commuter village?', 'A village where many residents travel to work in a nearby town or city.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is rural depopulation?', 'The decline in the population of rural areas as people move to cities.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is the impact of second homes in rural areas?', 'Higher house prices, fewer local services used year-round, and communities left empty.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is counter-urbanisation''s effect on rural areas?', 'Increased house prices, more traffic, and changes to village character.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is a green belt?', 'An area of protected land around a city where building is restricted.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is the housing crisis in the UK?', 'A shortage of affordable homes, especially in London and the south-east.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is affordable housing?', 'Housing sold or rented below market price for people on low incomes.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is sustainable transport in UK cities?', 'Buses, trams, cycling schemes and electric vehicle charging points.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.3', 'The UK''s Evolving Human Landscape', 'What is ethnic diversity in UK cities?', 'Cities like London and Birmingham have diverse populations from many backgrounds.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'How many investigations does Edexcel B require?', 'Two: one physical and one human.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What are the physical investigation options?', 'Coasts or rivers.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What are the human investigation options?', 'Dynamic urban areas or changing rural settlements.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is quantitative data?', 'Numerical data, e.g. measurements and counts.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is qualitative data?', 'Descriptive data, e.g. interviews, photographs and field sketches.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is an unfamiliar fieldwork question?', 'A question asking you to apply fieldwork skills to data or methods you have not seen before.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'How many fieldwork enquiries must you complete?', 'Two: one physical and one human, in contrasting environments.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What are the six stages of an enquiry?', 'Question, data collection, processing and presenting, analysing and explaining, conclusions, evaluation.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is a hypothesis?', 'A statement that can be tested and proved or disproved by an investigation.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is primary data?', 'Data you collect yourself during fieldwork.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is secondary data?', 'Data collected by others, e.g. census data, maps or Environment Agency records.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is random sampling?', 'Every item has an equal chance of being selected.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is systematic sampling?', 'Taking samples at regular intervals, e.g. every 10 m along a transect.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is stratified sampling?', 'Sampling sub-groups in proportion to their size in the population.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What does the Bradshaw model predict?', 'Width, depth, velocity and discharge increase downstream; gradient and particle size decrease.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'How do you measure river velocity simply?', 'Time a float over a set distance (e.g. 10 m) and repeat three times.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'Name two risks in river fieldwork.', 'Slipping or drowning, and waterborne disease such as Weil''s disease.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is an environmental quality survey?', 'A survey scoring places on features such as litter, graffiti and green space.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'Why are environmental quality surveys unreliable?', 'Scoring is subjective and varies between people.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'Which graph shows a relationship between two variables?', 'A scatter graph with a line of best fit.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is a choropleth map?', 'A map shaded in different intensities to show data values for areas.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is the mean?', 'The total of all values divided by the number of values.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is the median?', 'The middle value when data is placed in order.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is the mode?', 'The value that occurs most often.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is the range?', 'The difference between the highest and lowest values.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is the interquartile range?', 'The spread of the middle 50% of data — upper quartile minus lower quartile.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What is an anomaly?', 'A result that does not fit the general pattern.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What does correlation not prove?', 'Causation — another factor may cause both variables to change.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What should a fieldwork conclusion do?', 'Answer the original question using evidence from the results.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '2.4', 'Geographical Investigations', 'What does fieldwork evaluation involve?', 'Identifying problems with methods and data, their effects, and improvements.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is the biosphere?', 'The living layer of the Earth — all plants, animals and other organisms.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is a biome?', 'A large-scale ecosystem with a distinctive climate and vegetation.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What mainly controls where biomes are found?', 'Climate — temperature and precipitation.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Where are tropical rainforests found?', 'Near the Equator, between the Tropics — Amazon, Congo and South-East Asia.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Where are hot deserts found?', 'Around 30° north and south, where air sinks at the sub-tropical high.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Where is the taiga found?', 'Between about 50°N and 70°N across Canada, Alaska, Scandinavia and Russia.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'How does altitude affect ecosystems?', 'Temperature falls about 6.5°C per 1,000 m, creating bands of vegetation.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Name three local factors that affect ecosystems.', 'Altitude, rock type and soils, and drainage.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What are ecosystem services?', 'The benefits people get from ecosystems.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Name the four types of ecosystem service.', 'Provisioning (goods), regulating, supporting and cultural.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give three goods from the biosphere.', 'Food, timber and medicines (also fresh water and fibres).', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'How does the biosphere regulate the atmosphere?', 'Photosynthesis absorbs CO₂ and releases oxygen; forests and soils store carbon.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'How do forests reduce flooding?', 'Trees intercept rain and roots help water infiltrate the soil.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give a supporting service.', 'Nutrient cycling or soil formation.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give a cultural service.', 'Recreation, tourism or spiritual value.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'How many modern medicines come from plants?', 'About a quarter.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'How do indigenous people use the biosphere?', 'For food, shelter, medicines and culture, e.g. the Yanomami and Sámi.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give an example of commercial exploitation of the biosphere.', 'Clearing rainforest for palm oil, soya or cattle, or logging the taiga.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Why is demand for resources increasing?', 'Population growth, rising wealth and urbanisation.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What did Malthus argue?', 'Population grows geometrically but food arithmetically, so population will outstrip food.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What are Malthus''s positive checks?', 'Famine, disease and war, which reduce population.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What did Boserup argue?', 'Population pressure drives innovation, so food production increases — "necessity is the mother of invention".', 22),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give evidence for Boserup.', 'The Green Revolution — food production has outpaced population since 1960.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Give evidence for Malthus.', 'Regional famines, ~700 million undernourished, and limits to fresh water and soils.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is the tundra?', 'A cold, treeless biome near the Arctic with permafrost and low-growing plants.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'Which theory better explains today?', 'Boserup explains global food trends; Malthus warns of local and environmental limits.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is a food web?', 'A diagram showing how feeding relationships are linked in an ecosystem.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is a producer?', 'An organism that makes its own food through photosynthesis, e.g. plants.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is a consumer?', 'An organism that eats other organisms.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.1', 'People and the Biosphere', 'What is a decomposer?', 'An organism that breaks down dead material, releasing nutrients, e.g. fungi and bacteria.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Where is the taiga?', 'Between about 50°N and 70°N — Canada, Alaska, Scandinavia and Russia.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What is the taiga climate like?', 'Long, very cold winters, short mild summers and low precipitation.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What trees dominate the taiga?', 'Conifers — spruce, pine, fir and larch.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Why are taiga trees conical?', 'So snow slides off without breaking branches.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Why do taiga trees have needles?', 'To reduce water loss when the ground is frozen.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Where are most nutrients stored in the taiga?', 'In the litter, because cold slows decomposition.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are the Alberta oil sands?', 'Oil-bearing sands under Canadian boreal forest, mined by stripping forest and peat.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Name three threats to the taiga.', 'Logging, oil sands mining, and climate-driven wildfires and pests.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What is an ecosystem?', 'A community of living things interacting with each other and their non-living environment.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Where are tropical rainforests found?', 'Near the equator, e.g. the Amazon, Congo Basin and Southeast Asia.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What is the climate of a tropical rainforest?', 'Hot (about 27 °C) and wet all year, with over 2000 mm of rain.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are the layers of the rainforest?', 'Emergent layer, canopy, understorey and forest floor.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What is the canopy?', 'The dense layer of tree tops that absorbs most sunlight.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are buttress roots?', 'Large roots that support tall trees in shallow soils.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are drip tips?', 'Pointed leaves that allow heavy rain to run off quickly.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are lianas?', 'Woody vines that climb trees to reach sunlight.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What are epiphytes?', 'Plants that grow on other plants to reach light, e.g. orchids.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'How are animals adapted to the rainforest?', 'E.g. sloths move slowly and are camouflaged; monkeys have prehensile tails; frogs have sticky feet.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'What is the nutrient cycle in rainforests?', 'Nutrients are rapidly recycled from leaf litter to plants, so the soil is poor.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'Edexcel', 'gcse', '3.2', 'Forests under Threat', 'Why is rainforest soil infertile?', 'Heavy rain washes nutrients away (leaching), and nutrients are held in plants.', 20),
