  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What are the natural causes of climate change?', 'Changes in the Earth''s orbit, volcanic eruptions and variations in solar output.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is the evidence for climate change?', 'Rising global temperatures, melting ice caps, rising sea levels, and ice core records.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What do ice cores show?', 'Air bubbles trapped in ice show past levels of CO₂ and temperature.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What are the effects of climate change on the environment?', 'Rising sea levels, melting ice, more extreme weather, and loss of habitats.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What are the effects of climate change on people?', 'Flooding, food shortages, water shortages, and health problems.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is mitigation?', 'Reducing the causes of climate change, e.g. cutting emissions.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is adaptation?', 'Changing how we live to cope with the effects of climate change.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'Give examples of mitigation.', 'Renewable energy, planting trees, carbon capture, and international agreements.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'Give examples of adaptation.', 'Flood defences, drought-resistant crops, and changing farming practices.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is carbon capture and storage?', 'Capturing CO₂ from power stations and storing it underground.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is the Paris Agreement?', 'A 2015 international agreement to limit global warming to well below 2 °C.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is a carbon footprint?', 'The total amount of greenhouse gases produced by a person, organisation or activity.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'How can individuals reduce their carbon footprint?', 'Using public transport, saving energy, recycling, and eating less meat.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'How does climate change affect the UK?', 'Hotter summers, wetter winters, more flooding and rising sea levels.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'How does climate change affect poorer countries?', 'They are often more vulnerable to droughts, floods and storms, with fewer resources to adapt.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is sea-level rise caused by?', 'Melting ice sheets and glaciers, and thermal expansion of water.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is thermal expansion?', 'Water expanding as it warms, raising sea levels.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is the Quaternary period?', 'The last 2.6 million years, with glacial and interglacial periods.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is an interglacial period?', 'A warmer period between glacial periods.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'How does deforestation contribute to climate change?', 'Trees absorb CO₂; removing them increases CO₂ in the atmosphere.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is the role of methane in climate change?', 'Methane is a powerful greenhouse gas released by cattle, rice farming and landfill.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is renewable energy?', 'Energy from sources that won''t run out, e.g. wind, solar and hydroelectric power.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.3', 'Changing Climate', 'What is a climate refugee?', 'Someone forced to move because of the effects of climate change.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How does igneous rock form?', 'From cooled magma or lava — hard rocks such as granite and basalt.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How does sedimentary rock form?', 'From layers of sediment compressed over time, e.g. chalk, clay and limestone.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How does metamorphic rock form?', 'Existing rock changed by heat and pressure, e.g. slate and schist.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a Shoreline Management Plan?', 'A plan dividing the coast into sections, each given an option such as hold the line or managed realignment.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'Name the four SMP options.', 'Hold the line, advance the line, managed realignment and no active intervention.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'Why can coastal defences cause conflict?', 'They can starve beaches downdrift of sediment, increasing erosion elsewhere.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What are the four processes of coastal erosion?', 'Hydraulic action, abrasion, attrition and solution.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is hydraulic action?', 'Waves force air into cracks in the cliff, which breaks the rock apart.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is abrasion?', 'Rocks carried by waves are thrown against the cliff, wearing it away.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is attrition?', 'Rocks carried by waves knock against each other, becoming smaller and rounder.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is solution?', 'Seawater dissolves soluble rocks such as chalk and limestone.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is longshore drift?', 'The movement of sediment along the coast by waves approaching at an angle.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is the swash?', 'The movement of water up the beach after a wave breaks.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is the backwash?', 'The movement of water back down the beach under gravity.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a constructive wave?', 'A low, gentle wave with a strong swash and weak backwash, which builds up beaches.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a destructive wave?', 'A tall, steep wave with a weak swash and strong backwash, which erodes beaches.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is fetch?', 'The distance over which the wind blows across open water, affecting wave size.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How is a headland formed?', 'Resistant rock erodes more slowly than softer rock, leaving land sticking out into the sea.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How is a bay formed?', 'Softer rock is eroded more quickly, forming a curved inlet between headlands.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How is a stack formed?', 'Waves erode a crack into a cave, then an arch; the arch roof collapses, leaving a stack.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a stump?', 'The remains of a stack after it has been eroded further.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a wave-cut platform?', 'A flat area of rock at the base of a cliff, left as the cliff retreats through erosion.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'How is a spit formed?', 'Longshore drift carries sediment past a bend in the coastline, where it is deposited in the sea.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a bar?', 'A spit that grows across a bay, joining two headlands and sometimes trapping a lagoon.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a beach?', 'A deposit of sand and shingle along the coast, formed by constructive waves.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a sand dune?', 'A hill of sand formed when wind blows sand inland, trapped by vegetation such as marram grass.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is hard engineering?', 'Building artificial structures to control the sea, e.g. sea walls, groynes and rock armour.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is soft engineering?', 'Working with natural processes to manage the coast, e.g. beach nourishment and dune regeneration.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a sea wall?', 'A concrete wall that reflects waves back out to sea; effective but expensive.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.4', 'Distinctive Landscapes: UK Landscapes and Coasts', 'What is a groyne?', 'A wooden or rock barrier built out to sea to trap sediment moved by longshore drift.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is the source of a river?', 'Where the river begins, often in upland areas.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is the mouth of a river?', 'Where the river meets the sea or a lake.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a tributary?', 'A smaller river that joins a larger one.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a confluence?', 'The point where two rivers meet.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a drainage basin?', 'The area of land drained by a river and its tributaries.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a watershed?', 'The boundary of a drainage basin, usually high ground.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'How does a river change from source to mouth?', 'It becomes wider and deeper, with a greater discharge and gentler gradient.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is vertical erosion?', 'Erosion that deepens the river channel, common in the upper course.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is lateral erosion?', 'Erosion that widens the river channel, common in the middle and lower course.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What are the four types of river transportation?', 'Traction, saltation, suspension and solution.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is traction?', 'Large boulders are rolled along the river bed.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is saltation?', 'Small pebbles bounce along the river bed.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is suspension?', 'Fine particles are carried in the water.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'When does a river deposit sediment?', 'When it loses energy, e.g. when it slows down on the inside of a bend or enters the sea.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'How is a waterfall formed?', 'Soft rock beneath hard rock is eroded, creating an overhang that collapses; the waterfall retreats, leaving a gorge.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a gorge?', 'A steep-sided valley formed as a waterfall retreats upstream.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a V-shaped valley?', 'A steep valley in the upper course, formed by vertical erosion and weathering.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is interlocking spurs?', 'Hills that stick out alternately on either side of a river in the upper course.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'How is a meander formed?', 'Erosion on the outside of a bend (fast flow) and deposition on the inside (slow flow).', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'How is an oxbow lake formed?', 'Erosion narrows the neck of a meander until the river cuts through it during a flood; deposition seals off the old loop.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a floodplain?', 'Flat land either side of a river in the lower course, covered with deposits during floods.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a levée?', 'A raised bank along a river, formed by deposition of sediment during floods.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a hydrograph?', 'A graph showing river discharge over time, often in relation to rainfall.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is lag time?', 'The time between peak rainfall and peak discharge.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What factors increase flood risk?', 'Heavy rainfall, impermeable rock, steep slopes, urbanisation and deforestation.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'How does urbanisation increase flood risk?', 'Impermeable surfaces increase surface runoff, and drains carry water quickly to rivers.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a flood defence?', 'A structure or strategy to reduce flooding, e.g. dams, embankments, flood relief channels.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is a flood relief channel?', 'An artificial channel that diverts water away from a town when river levels are high.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is river restoration?', 'Returning a river to a more natural state to reduce flood risk and improve habitats.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.5', 'Distinctive Landscapes: Rivers', 'What is flood zoning?', 'Restricting building on floodplains in areas at high risk of flooding.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is an ecosystem?', 'A community of living things interacting with each other and their non-living environment.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a biome?', 'A large-scale ecosystem, e.g. tropical rainforest or hot desert.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'Where are tropical rainforests found?', 'Near the equator, e.g. the Amazon, Congo Basin and Southeast Asia.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the climate of a tropical rainforest?', 'Hot (about 27 °C) and wet all year, with over 2000 mm of rain.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the layers of the rainforest?', 'Emergent layer, canopy, understorey and forest floor.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the canopy?', 'The dense layer of tree tops that absorbs most sunlight.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are buttress roots?', 'Large roots that support tall trees in shallow soils.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are drip tips?', 'Pointed leaves that allow heavy rain to run off quickly.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are lianas?', 'Woody vines that climb trees to reach sunlight.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are epiphytes?', 'Plants that grow on other plants to reach light, e.g. orchids.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'How are animals adapted to the rainforest?', 'E.g. sloths move slowly and are camouflaged; monkeys have prehensile tails; frogs have sticky feet.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is the nutrient cycle in rainforests?', 'Nutrients are rapidly recycled from leaf litter to plants, so the soil is poor.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'Why is rainforest soil infertile?', 'Heavy rain washes nutrients away (leaching), and nutrients are held in plants.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is biodiversity?', 'The variety of living things in an area.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'Why do rainforests have high biodiversity?', 'Warm, wet climate all year allows plants to grow quickly, providing many habitats.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is deforestation?', 'The cutting down or removal of forests.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the causes of deforestation?', 'Logging, cattle ranching, farming (e.g. palm oil and soya), mining, road building and hydroelectric dams.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What are the impacts of deforestation?', 'Loss of biodiversity, soil erosion, climate change, and loss of indigenous people''s homes.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'How does deforestation contribute to climate change?', 'Trees store carbon; burning or cutting them releases CO₂, and fewer trees absorb CO₂.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is sustainable forestry?', 'Managing forests so trees are replanted and the forest can continue to provide resources.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is selective logging?', 'Only cutting down some mature trees, leaving the rest of the forest intact.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is ecotourism?', 'Tourism that conserves the environment and benefits local people.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is agroforestry?', 'Growing crops and trees together, protecting soil and providing resources.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is debt-for-nature swap?', 'A country''s debt is reduced in exchange for protecting its rainforest.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What role do indigenous people play in rainforests?', 'They often live sustainably and help protect forests from exploitation.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a food web?', 'A diagram showing how feeding relationships are linked in an ecosystem.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a producer?', 'An organism that makes its own food through photosynthesis, e.g. plants.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a consumer?', 'An organism that eats other organisms.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'What is a decomposer?', 'An organism that breaks down dead material, releasing nutrients, e.g. fungi and bacteria.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.6', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Tropical Rainforests', 'Why is the Amazon rainforest important globally?', 'It stores carbon, regulates climate, has huge biodiversity, and provides medicines.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How much fresh water is in the Antarctic ice sheet?', 'About 70% of the world''s fresh water.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Who discovered the ozone hole?', 'The British Antarctic Survey, in 1985.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Name three threats to Antarctica.', 'Climate change, tourism and overfishing.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What does IAATO do?', 'Regulates Antarctic tourism — e.g. no more than 100 people ashore at a site at once.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What does CCAMLR do?', 'Sets catch limits for krill and toothfish and created the Ross Sea Marine Protected Area.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why is Antarctica easier to manage than the Arctic?', 'It has no permanent population or national economy, and is governed by one treaty.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What are the two main types of cold environment?', 'Polar (ice sheets, e.g. Antarctica) and tundra (treeless land fringing the Arctic).', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Where is tundra found?', 'Roughly 60°–75°N in northern Canada, Alaska, northern Russia and Scandinavia.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What is permafrost?', 'Ground that stays frozen for at least two consecutive years.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What is the active layer?', 'The top layer of ground above the permafrost that thaws each summer.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why is the tundra waterlogged in summer?', 'Meltwater cannot drain through the impermeable permafrost below.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How cold do polar winters get?', 'Often below −50°C; Antarctica''s record is −89.2°C.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How much precipitation do polar areas get?', 'Under 250 mm a year — they are polar deserts.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why are polar areas so cold?', 'Low-angle sunlight is spread out and high-albedo snow and ice reflect most of it.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How long is the tundra growing season?', 'About 6–10 weeks.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why can''t trees grow in the tundra?', 'Permafrost stops roots growing deep and the summer is too short and cold.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why are tundra soils infertile?', 'They are thin, acidic and decomposition is very slow, so peat builds up.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How do plants protect permafrost?', 'Vegetation and peat insulate the ground from summer heat.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Give two plant adaptations to the tundra.', 'Low cushion shapes to avoid wind, and shallow roots in the active layer.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Give two animal adaptations to cold environments.', 'Thick fur or blubber for insulation, and small extremities to reduce heat loss.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why do caribou migrate?', 'To find food and avoid the harshest winter conditions — up to 5,000 km a year.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why is biodiversity low in cold environments?', 'The harsh climate allows few species, so food webs are simple.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why are cold environment food webs fragile?', 'With few species, losing one (e.g. lemmings) affects many others.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What is the main economic opportunity in Alaska?', 'Oil, especially from Prudhoe Bay on the North Slope.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What is the Alaska Permanent Fund?', 'A fund built from oil revenue that pays every resident an annual dividend.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Give two other opportunities in Alaska.', 'Fishing (about 60% of US seafood) and tourism (over 2 million visitors a year).', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Give two challenges of developing Alaska.', 'Extreme cold and inaccessibility — vast distances and few roads.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'Why are Alaskan buildings raised on piles?', 'To stop heat from the building thawing the permafrost and causing subsidence.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'How was the Trans-Alaska Pipeline designed?', 'Raised on supports with heat pipes, built in a zigzag, with crossings for caribou.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '1.7', 'Sustaining Ecosystems: Polar Environments', 'What happened in the Exxon Valdez disaster?', 'In 1989, about 41 million litres of oil spilled into Prince William Sound, killing wildlife.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is urbanisation?', 'The increase in the proportion of people living in towns and cities.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a megacity?', 'A city with a population of more than 10 million.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What causes urbanisation?', 'Rural–urban migration and natural increase.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What are push factors?', 'Reasons that make people leave rural areas, e.g. lack of jobs, poor services and natural disasters.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What are pull factors?', 'Reasons that attract people to cities, e.g. jobs, better healthcare and education.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is natural increase?', 'When the birth rate is higher than the death rate.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'Where is urbanisation happening fastest?', 'In lower-income and newly emerging countries in Africa and Asia.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a squatter settlement?', 'An area of poor-quality housing built illegally on land the residents don''t own.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What are the problems of squatter settlements?', 'Poor sanitation, lack of clean water, disease, crime, and flood or fire risk.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is the informal economy?', 'Jobs that aren''t officially recorded or taxed, e.g. street selling.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a site-and-service scheme?', 'Authorities provide land with basic services, and residents build their own homes.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is self-help housing?', 'Residents are given materials and support to improve their own homes.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is suburbanisation?', 'The movement of people from the inner city to the suburbs.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is counter-urbanisation?', 'The movement of people from cities to rural areas.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is re-urbanisation?', 'The movement of people back into city centres, often after regeneration.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a global city?', 'A city with major international influence in finance, culture and politics, e.g. London or New York.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What are the challenges of rapid urbanisation?', 'Housing shortages, traffic, pollution, unemployment and pressure on services.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is urban sprawl?', 'The spread of cities into the surrounding countryside.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a brownfield site?', 'Previously developed land that can be reused.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a greenfield site?', 'Land that hasn''t been built on before.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is a sustainable city?', 'A city that meets people''s needs without damaging the environment for future generations.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'Give an example of a sustainable urban feature.', 'Public transport, green spaces, recycling schemes and energy-efficient buildings.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is the CBD?', 'The central business district, the commercial centre of a city.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is the inner city?', 'The area around the CBD, often with older housing and industry.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is the rural–urban fringe?', 'The area where the city meets the countryside.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is gentrification?', 'Wealthier people moving into a poorer area and improving properties, which can displace original residents.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is regeneration?', 'Improving a run-down area through investment in housing, jobs and services.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What are the benefits of urbanisation?', 'Better access to jobs, education and healthcare, and economic growth.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'What is an urban transport problem?', 'Traffic congestion, which causes pollution and delays.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.1', 'Urban Futures', 'How can urban transport problems be reduced?', 'Park-and-ride, congestion charges, bus lanes, cycle lanes and trams.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is an AC?', 'An Advanced Country — high income and HDI, e.g. the UK.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is an EDC?', 'An Emerging and Developing Country — rapid growth and industrialisation, e.g. China or Brazil.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is an LIDC?', 'A Low-Income Developing Country — low income and HDI, mostly farming, e.g. Ethiopia.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'Where is Ethiopia?', 'A landlocked country in the Horn of Africa; capital Addis Ababa.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'Give two development indicators for Ethiopia.', 'GNI per capita about $1,000 and HDI about 0.49.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'Give two obstacles to Ethiopia''s development.', 'Drought affecting rain-fed farming, and conflict (Tigray 2020–22).', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is the Grand Ethiopian Renaissance Dam?', 'Africa''s largest HEP project on the Blue Nile — a top-down scheme.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is the Productive Safety Net Programme?', 'Cash or food for work on community projects for ~8 million people — a bottom-up scheme.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What does Rostow''s model show?', 'Five stages of economic growth: traditional society to high mass consumption.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'Name Rostow''s five stages.', 'Traditional society, pre-conditions for take-off, take-off, drive to maturity, high mass consumption.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'Give a criticism of Rostow''s model.', 'It is based on Western countries and ignores colonialism and unequal trade.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is Frank''s dependency theory?', 'A rich core keeps the poor periphery underdeveloped through unequal trade, debt and aid.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What does the Gini coefficient measure?', 'Income inequality within a country, from 0 (equal) to 1 (unequal).', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is top-down vs bottom-up development?', 'Top-down: large government-led projects; bottom-up: small community-led projects.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is development?', 'The process of improving people''s standard of living and quality of life.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is GNI per capita?', 'Gross national income divided by the population, a measure of average wealth.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is the Human Development Index?', 'A measure of development combining life expectancy, education and income.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is life expectancy?', 'The average number of years a person is expected to live.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is literacy rate?', 'The percentage of adults who can read and write.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is infant mortality rate?', 'The number of babies who die before their first birthday per 1000 live births.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is a low-income country (LIDC)?', 'A poorer country with lower development, e.g. Malawi.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is the development gap?', 'The difference in wealth and quality of life between richer and poorer countries.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What are the causes of uneven development?', 'Physical factors (climate, disasters), economic factors (trade, debt) and historical factors (colonialism).', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'How does trade affect development?', 'Countries exporting low-value primary products earn less than those exporting manufactured goods.', 24),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is aid?', 'Help given by one country or organisation to another, e.g. money, food or expertise.', 25),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is short-term aid?', 'Emergency help after a disaster, e.g. food, shelter and medicine.', 26),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is long-term aid?', 'Help to improve development over time, e.g. building schools and wells.', 27),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is fair trade?', 'A system ensuring producers in poorer countries receive a fair price and good working conditions.', 28),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is debt relief?', 'Cancelling some of a country''s debt so it can spend more on development.', 29),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.2', 'Dynamic Development', 'What is microfinance?', 'Small loans to people in poorer countries to start businesses.', 30),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What was the UK population in 2023?', 'About 69 million.', 1),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'Why is the UK population growing?', 'Natural increase and, mainly, net international migration.', 2),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What share of the UK is aged 65+?', 'Over 18%.', 3),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'Why is the UK population ageing?', 'Falling birth rates and longer life expectancy.', 4),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'Give two impacts of an ageing population.', 'More pressure on health care and pensions; fewer workers per retired person.', 5),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is the "grey pound"?', 'The spending power of older people.', 6),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'How does the UK influence the world culturally?', 'Through the BBC, films, TV, music and the Premier League.', 7),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'Name three international organisations the UK belongs to.', 'The UN Security Council (permanent member), G7 and NATO.', 8),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is a core region?', 'An area with high population, jobs and income, e.g. London and the South East.', 9),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is a peripheral region?', 'A remote area with low population, fewer jobs and ageing population, e.g. the Scottish Highlands.', 10),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What share of UK jobs are in services?', 'Over 80%.', 11),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'How has migration affected UK population?', 'It is a major part of population growth and brings a younger workforce.', 12),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'How has online shopping affected high streets?', 'Fewer shoppers and many shop closures.', 13),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'Give an example of an urban–rural link.', 'Commuting from villages into cities, or cities using rural reservoirs and recreation.', 14),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is the UK''s population distribution?', 'Most people live in cities and the south-east of England, with lower densities in upland areas.', 15),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is deindustrialisation?', 'The decline of manufacturing industry.', 16),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What caused deindustrialisation in UK cities?', 'Competition from cheaper overseas producers, automation, and the decline of coal and steel.', 17),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is the post-industrial economy?', 'An economy based on services, finance, research and IT rather than manufacturing.', 18),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is a science park?', 'A group of high-tech businesses located near a university.', 19),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is urban deprivation?', 'A lack of access to jobs, services and good housing in parts of a city.', 20),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is the Index of Multiple Deprivation?', 'A measure of deprivation using income, employment, health, education, crime, housing and environment.', 21),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is urban regeneration?', 'Improving run-down urban areas to attract people and businesses.', 22),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What is Cardiff Bay regeneration?', 'Redevelopment of the old docks into a waterfront area with offices, housing, the Senedd and leisure facilities.', 23),
  ('Geography', 'OCR', 'gcse', '2.3', 'UK in the 21st Century', 'What are the benefits of regeneration?', 'New jobs, improved environment, better housing and increased investment.', 24),
